<repo-qa-task id="{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1" sprint="d-4" round="1">
  <description><![CDATA[QA round 1 of `{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4` (sprint d-4), layer 4 of stack `phase-d`. Operate under `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/roles/quality-mgr.md`.]]></description>

  <checked-bead><![CDATA[{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4]]></checked-bead>
  <phase><![CDATA[d]]></phase>
  <phase-feature><![CDATA[{{ bead_prefix }}-phase-d]]></phase-feature>
  <stack><![CDATA[phase-d]]></stack>
  <layer><![CDATA[4]]></layer>
  <pr-number><![CDATA[231]]></pr-number>
  <branch><![CDATA[sprint/d-4-otlp-sync-exporter]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d]]></commit>
  <base><![CDATA[sprint/d-3-otlp-config]]></base>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_base }}/sprint/d-4-otlp-sync-exporter]]></worktree>
  <carry-forward><![CDATA[]]></carry-forward>
  <stack-discipline><![CDATA[`sprint/d-4-otlp-sync-exporter` is frozen at `4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d` for this review. Every reviewer gets the same branch, commit, and worktree and must reject a mismatched or moving checkout. Review exact content with `git show 4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d:<path>`. The change under review is `git diff origin/sprint/d-3-otlp-config...4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d`, never a diff against a moving base. Every round-1 finding, at every severity, is filed in that round (blocking as a poured fix group, others as finding beads); none is deferred. Each is fixed later on a new layer at the top of stack `phase-d`. A fix-verification round checks only its carried findings against their original acceptance criteria and files no new findings.]]></stack-discipline>

  <fix-verification-precedence><![CDATA[A fix-verification review is not a sprint review, regardless of round number or inherited review-mode. Dispatch only the agent needed to confirm the original finding, normally its filing reviewer; no automatic req-qa/arch-qa/rust-qa or screening panel. Lock scope to the assigned finding ID and its original acceptance criterion; no sprint diff, TODO scan, duplicate sweep, or new findings. The verifier may run focused checks to confirm the fix. Report fixed/open/regressed for that finding and reconcile verified original-finding closure, not just QA-task closure. Required CI remains a separate merge requirement. This rule overrides the sprint-only instructions in stack-discipline and workflow steps c, e, g, and i. Sprint rounds 1–2 remain sprint reviews.]]></fix-verification-precedence>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Before claiming, run `bd ready -n 0 --json | jq --arg b {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1 'any(.[]; .id == $b)'`; if it prints `false` follow a2. Then run `gh pr view 231 --json baseRefName,headRefOid --jq '.baseRefName + " " + .headRefOid'`, `bd list -l stage:dev-sanity --status closed -n 0 --json | jq -r --arg b {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4 '[.[] | select(.metadata.dev_bead == $b and ((.close_reason // "") | startswith("PASS at ")))] | max_by(.closed_at) | .close_reason // "" | ltrimstr("PASS at ")'` (sha of its latest sanity PASS), and `git rev-parse HEAD`. Refuse `SANITY_STALE` unless: the PR base is `<pr_target>` or its descendant (`git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/<pr_target> origin/<PR base>` exits 0), `<pr_target>` being this QA bead's `metadata.pr_target` when set (a Parallel Quick Fix), else `{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4`'s, else its sprint container's (`metadata.sprint_bead`); its head starts with that sanity PASS sha (skipped when this QA bead's `metadata.quick_fix` is true: a Parallel Quick Fix has no sanity check); and this worktree HEAD equals the PR head. A layer or quick fix without a QA PASS at its pinned head is not mergeable. On refusal before claiming, close the task `refused` with the step i1 template, leaving the bead unchanged and including `SANITY_STALE`, the command and failure evidence in `reason_md`. Otherwise claim and start this QA round.]]></step>
    <step id="a1"><![CDATA[QA tasks run concurrently. Right after the task start, run `atm task list --json`. Treat every open task assigned to you as live now. Run each task with its own background reviewers. Close each task when its verdict is ready. ATM allows one active task per agent today. When another task is active, claim the bead, do the work, and close the task without starting it.]]></step>
    <step id="a2"><![CDATA[When it prints `false` the bead is not ready: do not claim it or start the task. Find the root cause: `bd show {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1` (status, assignee), `bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1 '.[] | select(.id == $b)'` (normally its sanity bead still open), and `bd show <blocker>` for each. Then refuse; never wait: `atm task close {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1 refused --template .atm-bd/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-vars.json`, `bead_state` `open`, `reason_md` the bead, why it is not ready, which bead or agent has to move, and for a blocker not yet its dependency the edge to add, `bd dep add {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1 --blocked-by <blocker>`, so `bd ready` lists the bead only once the blocker closes. The task assigner re-assigns it then.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[If the assignment is not an XML payload rendered from this template, reject the task immediately. Read `.claude/project/quality-policy.md`. Write the reviewers' sprint input once, piping the checked bead in; it replaces the sprint doc and is passed to every reviewer as `sprint_doc`:
```bash
{ printf 'QA of {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4 (sprint d-4) at 4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d on sprint/d-4-otlp-sync-exporter; change = git diff origin/sprint/d-3-otlp-config...4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d.\n\n'
  printf 'The bead under review is the sprint plan: its description, design and acceptance criteria are the deliverables.\n\n```json\n'
  bd show {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4 --json | jq '.[0] | {id, title, description, design, acceptance_criteria, metadata}'
  printf '```\n'
  { bd show {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4 --json; bd show "$(bd show {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4 --json | jq -r '.[0].metadata.sprint_bead // .[0].id')" --json; } | jq -s -r '(.[0][0].metadata // {}) as $c | (.[1][0].metadata // {}) as $s | "\nGoverning requirements: \(($c.requirements // $s.requirements // ["MISSING"]) | join(", "))\nGoverning ADRs: \(($c.adrs // $s.adrs // ["MISSING"]) | join(", "))\nThe reviewers check the change against every listed id. NONE means the plan declares none: a change that touches a requirement or ADR anyway is a blocking finding, and so is MISSING. So is a listed id that its governing document does not define at this commit: a sprint that adds an id must land its definition.\n"'
} > <scratch>/{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-sprint.md
```
Render every selected reviewer's structured JSON assignment from `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/<reviewer>-assignment.json.j2`; if a reviewer has no template there, give it the fenced-JSON input its own contract, `.claude/agents/<reviewer>.md`, names (`rust-best-practices-agent` also gets `practice_mode` = `all`). Each assignment carries the exact branch `sprint/d-4-otlp-sync-exporter`, commit `4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d` and worktree `{{ worktree_base }}/sprint/d-4-otlp-sync-exporter`; if its assignment template takes it, also `sprint_doc` = `<scratch>/{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-sprint.md`. Render each as `roles/quality-mgr.md` ("Rendering") says. Do not send free-form reviewer prompts.]]></step>
    <step id="c"><![CDATA[Extract every deliverable, acceptance criterion, deletion requirement, required validation item, and expected artifact from the checked bead. Deliverable completion is `X/Y (Z%)`.]]></step>
    <step id="d"><![CDATA[This is a sprint review: run the full reviewer set, `req-qa`, `arch-qa`, `rust-qa-agent`, `ruthless-boundary-qa`, `rust-best-practices-agent` and `rust-service-hardening-agent`, plus the conditional reviewers `roles/quality-mgr.md` ("Reviewers") names when their condition holds, each with `qa_round` = 1. Spawn every selected reviewer in background. Do not run tests, linters, or broad QA analysis yourself in the foreground.]]></step>
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Collect reviewer outputs. Re-verify every cited file:line at `4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d` with `git show 4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d:<path>`, never a moving branch tip or worktree. Stale or missing evidence is a finding, not a guess. For each repeatable-pattern finding, search the whole commit for other occurrences and include all of them. A reviewer whose assignment takes `duplicate_sweep_symbols` gets every constant, function, or type the change touches, for a workspace-wide duplicate sweep.]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[Run `ceremony-finding-screen` (`.claude/agents/ceremony-finding-screen.md`) as a background agent over every finding of this round, with the fenced-JSON input its contract names: `worktree_path` = `{{ worktree_base }}/sprint/d-4-otlp-sync-exporter`, `sprint_doc` = `<scratch>/{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-sprint.md`, and `findings` = this round's findings.]]></step>
    <step id="f1"><![CDATA[For every blocking finding row written in step g, first read the checked bead's provenance with `bd show {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4 --json | jq -c '.[0].metadata | (.layer | select(. != null and . != "")) // (.found_on_layer | select(. != null and . != "")) // empty'` with pipefail enabled; stop on a failed read or malformed JSON. Add its value as `found_on_layer` to each row in the blocking JSON, both on an initial sprint review and on fix verification. If neither field is present, omit `found_on_layer`; never substitute the sprint container's layer.]]></step>
    <step id="g"><![CDATA[File every finding, screened or not. A blocking finding the screen keeps is poured, not filed as a finding bead: list each in `<scratch>/{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-blocking.json` = `{"sprint": "<the checked bead's metadata.sprint_bead>", "round": 1, "filed_by": "{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1", "found_at_commit": "4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d", "findings": [{"ref": "qa1-f<n>", "severity": "blocking", "reviewer": "<reviewer>", "title": "<title>", "remedy": "<remedy>", "priority": 1, "difficulty": "<difficulty>"}]}` and run `.atm-bd/scripts/bead-groups --findings <scratch>/{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-blocking.json` (`difficulty` is optional; omitted, the sprint's applies); each pours a fix ← sanity ← qa group under the sprint; a nonzero exit stops the round (fix the file, rerun). When this QA bead's `metadata.quick_fix` is true, write that file but do not run `bead-groups`: list each blocking finding in the close's `findings_md` for the task assigner, who files each as a finding bead and dispatches it to an idle roster agent (`SKILL.md` Parallel Quick Fix step 4); it fails the round. File every other finding (important, minor, or screened `ceremony`) with `.atm-bd/templates/finding-bead.json.j2`: `id` = `{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-f<n>`, `qa_bead` = `{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1`, `parent` = `{{ bead_prefix }}-phase-d`, `stack` = `phase-d`, `found_on_layer` = `4`, `found_at_commit` = `4f1c2a9e7b3d5f60812a4c9e0b7d3f5a1c2e4b6d`, the screen verdict, and the contract copied from the checked bead: `requirements` and `adrs` = its `metadata.requirements` and `metadata.adrs` (a poured dev bead has none: use its sprint container's), `sprint_bead` = its `metadata.sprint_bead` for a finding or its own id for a dev bead (`bd show {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4 --json | jq '.[0] | {id, sprint_bead: (.metadata.sprint_bead // .id), requirements: .metadata.requirements, adrs: .metadata.adrs}'`, then `bd show <sprint_bead> --json | jq '.[0].metadata | {requirements, adrs}'` for a null). Normalize severity first: `critical`, `Blocking` and `BLOCKING` → `blocking`; `Important`/`IMPORTANT` → `important`; `Minor`/`MINOR`/`low` → `minor`. Render each to a file and gate it, so a rejected finding stops the round instead of vanishing: `sc-compose render --file <template> --var-file <vars> --strict --output <scratch>/<finding>.json && jq -e -c . <scratch>/<finding>.json >> <scratch>/{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-findings.jsonl` (any failure: fix the vars and re-render; never skip the finding). Then `bd import <scratch>/{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-findings.jsonl`. Apply the screen per `roles/quality-mgr.md` ("Findings"); close a `ceremony` finding at once with `bd close <finding> --reason "ceremony: <reason>"`.]]></step>
    <step id="g1"><![CDATA[After step g, verify it added only fix groups, finding beads and declared inter-finding prerequisites. Do not add a finding-derived edge to a planned sprint: the phase's plan file is the minimum set of sprint dependency edges, and only the lead adds one (even one discovered in motion); recommend it in the report.]]></step>
    <step id="h"><![CDATA[Post the report on PR 231 before closing: `atm compose --template .atm-bd/templates/qa-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/qa-{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-vars.json | gh pr comment 231 --body-file -`. Check stack and CI state with the `sc-gh-stack-view` skill and `gh pr checks 231 --json name,state,bucket`; never `--watch`, never parse its text output.]]></step>
    <step id="i"><![CDATA[Close this review through .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/atm-task-close.py --role qa --vars <shared-vars.json>. Pour the fix groups before invoking it. PASS requires 100% deliverable completion, a PASS from every required reviewer, and no blocking or important finding filed open this round. The hook closes the QA bead first, closes the task only if that succeeds, and sends the phase lead one status report for PASS and FAIL alike. It assigns no dev or fix. On err, fix the named cause and rerun the same hook.]]></step>
    <step id="i1"><![CDATA[If the review cannot be performed, include the reason, command and failure evidence in the refusal's `reason_md`. Also announce a serious infrastructure failure once per cause to the oversight recipients (`.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/SKILL.md` Lead Role). Return the bead with `bd update {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1 --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "QA_CANNOT_RUN; <reason>"` and close the task with `atm task close {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1 refused --template .atm-bd/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-vars.json`. A blocker is not a failure: when a prerequisite reopens or the work needs an unlanded fix, stop, return the bead with `bd update {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1 --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why>"` and close the task `refused` as above (`bead_state` `open`), its `reason_md` naming the blocker and the edge `bd dep add {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1 --blocked-by <blocker>`; never stay active waiting.]]></step>
    <step id="j"><![CDATA[After step i's closes succeed (never on the i1 refusal path — no round to log), append exactly one row to each of the two phase QA logs under `.sc/qa-log/`, per `roles/quality-mgr.md` ("QA Metrics Log"). Compute both rows fresh at close time; never hand-carry a prior row's numbers:
```bash
mkdir -p .sc/qa-log
# Each row is built first and appended with one printf: a single O_APPEND write, atomic without a lock.

CREATED=$(bd show {{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1 --json | jq -r '.[0].created_at')
C_EPOCH=$(date -u -j -f "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ" "$CREATED" +%s 2>/dev/null || date -u -d "$CREATED" +%s)
NOW_EPOCH=$(date -u +%s)
NOW=$(date -u -r "$NOW_EPOCH" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ 2>/dev/null || date -u -d "@$NOW_EPOCH" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
LOCAL=$(date +%H:%M)
SECS=$((NOW_EPOCH - C_EPOCH))
DURATION="$((SECS/60))m$(printf '%02d' $((SECS%60)))s"

FNDFILE=<scratch>/{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-findings.jsonl
BLKFILE=<scratch>/{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1-blocking.json
BLK=$( [ -f "$BLKFILE" ] && jq '.findings | length' "$BLKFILE" || echo 0 )
IMP=$( [ -f "$FNDFILE" ] && jq -sc '[.[] | select(.metadata.screen!="ceremony" and .metadata.severity=="important")] | length' "$FNDFILE" || echo 0 )
MIN=$( [ -f "$FNDFILE" ] && jq -sc '[.[] | select(.metadata.screen!="ceremony" and .metadata.severity=="minor")] | length' "$FNDFILE" || echo 0 )
FND=$((BLK + IMP + MIN))
TESTED="{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4"

ROW=$(jq -nc --arg completed_at "$NOW" --arg completed_local "$LOCAL" --arg duration "$DURATION" \
  --arg phase "d" --arg sprint "d-4" --arg task "{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1" \
  --arg pr_number "231" --argjson iteration 1 --arg verdict "$VERDICT" \
  --arg tested "$TESTED" --argjson fnd "$FND" --argjson blk "$BLK" --argjson imp "$IMP" --argjson min "$MIN" \
  '{completed_at:$completed_at, completed_local:$completed_local, duration:$duration, phase:$phase, sprint:$sprint,
    task:$task, pr_number:(($pr_number|tonumber?)//null), iteration:$iteration, verdict:$verdict, tested:$tested,
    fnd:$fnd, blk:$blk, imp:$imp, min:$min}')
printf '%s\n' "$ROW" >> .sc/qa-log/phase-d.jsonl

STATS=$(bd list --all --json 2>/dev/null | jq -c --arg ph "d" --arg completed_at "$NOW" --arg completed_local "$LOCAL" --arg task "{{ bead_prefix }}-d-4-qa1" '
  [.[] | select(.metadata.phase == $ph)] as $all |
  ([$all[] | select((.labels // []) | index("stage:finding")) | select(.metadata.sanity_finding | not)]
   + ([$all[] | select((.labels // []) | index("stage:fix"))]
      | group_by([.metadata.sprint_bead, .metadata.finding_ref]) | map(max_by(.metadata.round)))) as $f |
  {snapshot_at: $completed_at, snapshot_local: $completed_local, phase: $ph, trigger_task: $task,
   tot: ($f | length),
   open: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open")] | length),
   blk: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open" and .metadata.severity=="blocking")] | length),
   imp: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open" and .metadata.severity=="important")] | length),
   min: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open" and .metadata.severity=="minor")] | length)}')
printf '%s\n' "$STATS" >> .sc/qa-log/phase-d-stats.jsonl
```
Before running it, set `$VERDICT` to the `PASS`/`FAIL` value in step i's `bd close` reason. Never commit these logs from a QA worktree; the lead's phase-end housekeeping stages them.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</repo-qa-task>
